        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate the integral $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{e}^{e^{2}}\\frac{2}{5\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\operatorname{ln}({\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln\\left(\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)^{2}\\right).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{e}^{e^{2}}\\frac{2}{5\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\operatorname{ln}({\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{e}^{e^{2}}\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}({\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{2}^{4}\\frac{2}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}Abs(u))\\right)|_{2}^{4} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}4-\\operatorname{ln}2)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}{2}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}2)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{5}(2\\operatorname{ln}2-\\operatorname{ln}2)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}2}{5}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
